<task id="AIR2-044" project="spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Wire the confirmation gate on RISK + AMBIGUITY (not origin-provenance) — make Policy v2 live end-to-end, no shims</title>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <phase>Wave J — G-R2-A Judgment + Friction (gap-closer, re-scoped 2026-07-09 after operator reframing)</phase>
    <gate>G-R2-A</gate>
    <estimated-effort>1.5 days</estimated-effort>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Highest-blast-radius task of the wave: makes the deterministic confirmation gate LIVE on the core chat execution path with the real (tier × completeness × ambiguity) signals. A subtle shim (defaulting the ambiguity signal) would pass "code written" but fail "feature works end to end." Strongest reasoning + rigorous end-to-end verification required.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <effort-reason>Brownfield root-cause wiring across dispatch → gate → engine → behavior; the real ambiguity/confidence signal must be traced and threaded, not stubbed.</effort-reason>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <goal-eligible>false</goal-eligible>
    <tags>bff-api, ai, gate, confirmation-policy, judgment, ambiguity, end-to-end, no-shim</tags>
    <dependencies>032 (ConfirmationPolicyEngine PRODUCER + tier table + overlay precedence — MERGED, REUSED), 034 (gate pre-suspend validation — MERGED), 012 (GateDecisionV2 contract — MERGED), 040 (HandoffUrlBuilder deep-links — MERGED, reused for email handoff), 035 (Completion Engine / OutcomeCard — MERGED, carries the deep link + Undo).</dependencies>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Make the confirmation gate LIVE on the core chat path, driven by RISK + AMBIGUITY — NOT the E-1..E-6 "explicit vs inferred" origin-provenance machinery. Prior task-044 attempt correctly escalated (CLAUDE.md §6.5): the origin classifier's "Explicit" verdict has NO production producer (Click doesn't reach the LLM-loop gate; deriving Explicit from the utterance = ADR-039-banned re-parse), so it resolves Inferred 100%. The operator reframed the real problem (2026-07-09): confirmation is intrusive when the user CLEARLY asked ("yes, I just told you to create a task"); the genuine risk is an AMBIGUOUS instruction ("create a to do task" — a to-do or a task?) executing the wrong choice.

    THE MODEL (operator-ratified). Two layers:
    (1) The AGENT TURN handles ambiguity (ADR-039's sanctioned intent decider): when genuinely torn between capabilities, it ASKS a clarifying question instead of dispatching. Wrong-choice risk is caught here, before the gate.
    (2) The GATE handles risk, using ONLY real signals:
        - TIER (catalog DATA, real): 0/1 → execute (reads/drafts free, D-F0(b)); 2a/2b + complete → EXECUTE + Undo, NO dialog; 2c → preview/confirm (r2 default); 3/4 irreversible in-system (delete/supersede, set-deadline, assign-to-another-user) → ALWAYS confirm.
        - COMPLETENESS (real): incomplete args → the agent ELICITS (a natural question, not a scary confirm), then re-evaluate.
        - AMBIGUITY / dispatchUncertain overlay (real): a tool call flagged low-confidence → confirm (backstop on top of layer 1).
    Reuse ConfirmationPolicyEngine's tier table + overlay precedence AS-IS; feed its origin/confidence slot from the REAL ambiguity signal (confident → proceed for low-risk; uncertain → confirm). Do NOT build E-1..E-6 origin producers or any utterance-parser.

    EMAIL IS DRAFT + HANDOFF, NEVER AUTO-SEND (r2, operator-ratified): an email action DRAFTS the email (Tier 1, executes) and returns an OutcomeCard with a HandoffUrlBuilder deep link to open the email record for human review/edit/send. The human's review-and-send at that record IS the gate — NO confirm dialog, and the system NEVER sends. Auto-send (a true Tier-4 send side effect needing a confirm) is explicitly DEFERRED past r2.

    ABSOLUTE QUALITY MANDATE (operator, 2026-07-09): NO dead-ends, shims, pseudocode, or incomplete paths. The bar is "the feature works END TO END and is observable," not "did we write the code." The ambiguity/confidence signal MUST come from a real source — do NOT default/hardcode it. If no honest source exists, STOP and ESCALATE per §6.5 (as the prior attempt correctly did) rather than shim.
  </prompt>

  <role>Senior BFF engineer fluent in the ADR-039 dispatch model + closed catalog, the SprkChatAgentFactory gate wrap-site, the ADR-040 ledger / Gate status, the Policy v2 engine (tier table + overlay precedence), the Completion Engine/OutcomeCard + HandoffUrlBuilder deep-link pattern, and the SideEffectGateAIFunction suspend/resume lifecycle.</role>

  <goal>
    The confirmation gate is LIVE on the core chat path and driven by real (tier × completeness × ambiguity) signals via the reused ConfirmationPolicyEngine, REPLACING the old declared-class-only decision. Observable end-to-end: a clear+complete low-risk request (create-task, 2b) EXECUTES with no dialog + an Undo affordance; an email action drafts + returns a review/send deep link (no dialog, no auto-send); an ambiguous instruction makes the AGENT ask a clarifying question (no wrong-choice execution); an incomplete request elicits then re-evaluates; an irreversible in-system action (delete/supersede/deadline/assign) always confirms. The 034 pre-suspend validation, the R5-E hard block, Tier-0 free reads, and the fail-closed default (unknown/uncertain → confirm) are all preserved.
  </goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="reframing-decision">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/notes/044-signal-flow-trace.md (prior attempt's signal trace + escalation evidence)</file>
    <file purpose="policy-source">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r2/notes/policy-v2-origin-classification-decision-tree.md (tier table + overlay precedence — REUSE the tier/overlay parts; the E-1..E-6 origin parsing is OUT of scope now)</file>
    <file purpose="engine">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/Gate/ConfirmationPolicyEngine.cs</file>
    <file purpose="risk-resolver">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/Gate/RiskTierResolver.cs</file>
    <file purpose="gate-callsite">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/SideEffectGateAIFunction.cs</file>
    <file purpose="wrap-site">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Chat/SprkChatAgentFactory.cs</file>
    <file purpose="routing">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts (IConsumerRoutingService + routing — candidate-match ambiguity source to investigate)</file>
    <file purpose="handoff-links">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Agent/HandoffUrlBuilder.cs</file>
    <file purpose="completion">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/CompletionEngine.cs</file>
    <file purpose="adr">docs/adr/ADR-041-judgment-confirmation-completion-policy.md</file>
  </inputs>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="no-shim">The ambiguity/confidence signal MUST come from a real source. It MUST NOT be hardcoded/defaulted to fabricate a positive "explicit/confident" verdict. IMPORTANT — this is NOT an escalation trap: the operator's PRIMARY goal (a clear + complete low-risk request executes with NO dialog) is driven entirely by TIER + COMPLETENESS, which are BOTH already real (RiskTierResolver over catalog DATA + schema required[] vs args). Deliver that happy path first. Ambiguity ("create a to do task") is handled by LAYER 1 — the agent turn asking a clarifying question (real behavior, ADR-039's decider) — BEFORE the gate. The gate-side dispatchUncertain overlay is an OPTIONAL BACKSTOP: wire it to honor a real low-confidence signal IF one exists (e.g. a routing candidate-match count), but it may honestly remain unfired when there is no such signal — that is correct, not a shim, because layer 1 already covers ambiguity. Escalate per §6.5 ONLY if TIER or COMPLETENESS themselves cannot be sourced (they can) — do NOT escalate merely because dispatchUncertain lacks a strong producer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="no-origin-machinery">Do NOT build E-1..E-6 origin producers, a SessionGate.Origin field, a proposal-recording provenance system, or any utterance→action re-parse. The origin/confidence slot is fed by the real ambiguity signal, not parsed authorization provenance.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">Ambiguity is resolved by the AGENT TURN (asking a clarifying question) — the sanctioned intent decider. The gate adds no second intent mechanism. Risk tier stays catalog-declared DATA.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">Confirmation state is a Gate-ledger property; store-before-render preserved (suspend marker lands before any dialog render).</constraint>
    <constraint source="email-draft-handoff">Email = draft (executes) + OutcomeCard HandoffUrlBuilder deep link to open the email record for human review/edit/send. NO confirm dialog for the draft; NO auto-send in r2. Auto-send is deferred.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-F0(b)">Tier-0 reads/searches never gated; the gate only ever adds friction for risk/ambiguity, never weakens a hard block; a doomed call (034) still renders honest ❌ with affordance.</constraint>
    <constraint source="replace-not-shadow">The engine becomes the single top-level decider on the live path — do not leave the old declared-class-only decision as a parallel decider that can disagree.</constraint>
    <constraint source="bff-hygiene">Load .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md. Report publish-size delta (baseline ~46.48 MB compressed incl PDB; ceiling 60 MB) + no new HIGH CVE (pre-existing Microsoft.Kiota.Abstractions HIGH is not yours). ADR-013 facade discipline.</constraint>
    <constraint source="eval-gate">Golden-utterance + resourcefulness + origin eval families stay green. NOTE: the origin eval family (033) tests the engine's tier/overlay logic on constructed inputs — it stays valid; do not delete it. Add behavior cases for the newly-observable execute/confirm/elicit/ambiguity outcomes.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Confirm real inputs + trace the ambiguity signal">Confirm from actual code that TIER (RiskTierResolver over catalog DATA) and COMPLETENESS (schema required[] vs args) are sourceable at the gate call-site — they are; the happy path (clear+complete low-risk → execute no-dialog) rides these alone. Then investigate the OPTIONAL ambiguity backstop: does the routing (IConsumerRoutingService) expose a candidate-match count or a low-confidence flag the gate can honor? Update notes/044-signal-flow-trace.md. Do NOT escalate merely because the dispatchUncertain backstop lacks a strong producer (layer 1 — the agent asking — covers ambiguity). Escalate ONLY if tier or completeness themselves cannot be sourced.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Wire real inputs to the engine">At the live gate call-site (SideEffectGateAIFunction.InvokeCoreAsync), assemble the PolicyEvaluationContext from REAL signals: tier (RiskTierResolver over catalog DATA), completeness (schema required[] vs args / ValidateForGate), ambiguity (Step 0 signal → the origin/confidence slot: confident→proceed, uncertain→confirm), overlays. Call ConfirmationPolicyEngine.Evaluate. Replace the old declared-class-only decision.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Agent asks on ambiguity">Ensure the agent turn asks a clarifying question when genuinely torn between capabilities (directive/prompt + closed-catalog behavior) rather than dispatching a guess — this is layer 1. The dispatchUncertain overlay is the gate-side backstop.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Drive behavior from the decision">Tier 0/1 → execute; 2a/2b + confident + complete → execute + Undo (OutcomeCard Undo chip); 2c → preview/confirm; 3/4 irreversible in-system → confirm dialog; incomplete → elicit once then re-evaluate. EMAIL → draft executes + OutcomeCard HandoffUrlBuilder review/send deep link, no dialog, no send. Preserve 034 pre-suspend + R5-E hard block ahead of the decision.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Integration proof (anti-shim gate)">Integration tests on the REAL gate path (not a mocked engine) asserting OBSERVABLE behavior: (i) clear+complete Tier-2b create → executes, NO suspend marker, NO dialog, Undo present; (ii) email action → draft executes + OutcomeCard carries a review/send deep link, NO suspend marker, NO auto-send; (iii) ambiguous instruction → agent asks a clarifying question, NO side-effect executed; (iv) incomplete args → elicits once then re-evaluates; (v) irreversible in-system (delete/supersede or set-deadline) → exactly one suspend marker (one dialog); (vi) uncertain/unknown → confirm (fail-closed); (vii) R5-E hard block → honest ❌ with affordance, zero Dataverse writes. Each must fail if the ambiguity signal is hardcoded.</step>
    <step order="5" name="Eval + gates">Keep eval families green; add behavior cases. code-review + adr-check (Step 9.5). Report publish size + CVE.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">build + test</tool>
    <tool name="git">commit is MAIN-SESSION only — report proposed TASK-INDEX/current-task changes, do not commit yourself</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">The live gate call-site invoking ConfirmationPolicyEngine.Evaluate with real (tier × completeness × ambiguity) signals + decision-driven behavior</output>
    <output type="code">Email draft + OutcomeCard review/send deep link (HandoffUrlBuilder) — no auto-send</output>
    <output type="doc">notes/044-signal-flow-trace.md updated with the real ambiguity-signal source</output>
    <output type="test">Integration tests proving the 7 observable behaviors on the real gate path</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">ConfirmationPolicyEngine.Evaluate is invoked on the live core gate path for every side-effect tool invocation (real call-site, not a comment), fed real tier + completeness + ambiguity signals.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The ambiguity/confidence signal comes from a REAL source (documented in the trace) — NOT hardcoded/defaulted. No E-1..E-6 origin producer or utterance re-parse is built.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Observable behaviors proven by integration tests on the real gate path (mocking the engine is NOT acceptable proof): clear+complete 2b executes no-dialog + Undo; email drafts + review/send deep link with no dialog/no send; ambiguous → agent asks; incomplete → elicit; irreversible in-system → confirm once; uncertain → confirm.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The engine is the single top-level decider on the live path — the old declared-class-only decision is replaced/subsumed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Preserved: 034 pre-suspend validation (doomed → honest ❌ + affordance), R5-E hard block (zero Dataverse writes), Tier-0 free reads, fail-closed default (unknown/uncertain → confirm).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build 0 errors; golden-utterance + resourcefulness + origin eval families green; publish &lt; 60 MB; no new HIGH CVE; code-review + adr-check clean.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE / anti-shim: no path defaults/hardcodes the ambiguity signal; no TODO/NotImplemented/pseudocode in the live gate path; email is NEVER auto-sent in r2; the integration tests would FAIL if the ambiguity signal were faked.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the capability-selection ambiguity/confidence signal genuinely has no honest source reachable from the routing/agent-turn and cannot be produced within scope, STOP and escalate per §6.5 (describe the missing signal + the real source that would need to emit it + scope). Do NOT default it and call it done.</trigger>
    <trigger>If wiring surfaces a genuine ADR-039 (second intent mechanism) or ADR-040 (confirmation-state store) conflict that comply (Path C) cannot resolve, STOP and run the §6.5 protocol.</trigger>
  </escalation>
</task>
